 "figures": {
  "over-time": {
   "title": "The largest, over a world's life",
   "caption": "After every game of the 30 worlds. Left: the tokens of the richest agent, the largest gain and the largest loss of one agent in that game, and the tokens of the mean agent, each as a share of all 100,000 tokens. Right: the connections of the best-connected agent, of the mean agent and of the median one. Both on logarithmic axes; the line is the median of the worlds at each iteration, the darker band holds the middle half of them (from the 25th to the 75th percentile) and the paler band nine in ten (5th to 95th).",
   "recipe": "**Runs.** The 30 baseline runs `B1-100000-s001` \u2026 `B1-100000-s030`: the baseline B1 at 100,000 tokens, seeds 1 to 30, 1,500 iterations each (every setting is listed in Chapter 9). They are made with `python3 gol_lab.py run E10`.\n\n**Data.** From each run's `GraphOfLifeRuns/<run>/stats.jsonl`, which holds one row per recorded phase: `phase` 1 is the world just after reproduction, `phase` 2 just after the game, and every statistic is a field of the row (see [What a run records](../notes/frames-and-stats.md)).\n\n1. Take the rows with `phase` = 2: `maxTokens`, `maxTokenAdded`, `maxTokenLost` and `meanTokens`, divided by 100,000; `maxDegree`, `meanDegree` and `medianDegree`.\n2. Cut the 1,500 iterations into 600 stretches of 2.5 and take each world's mean in each stretch.\n3. In each stretch, take the median, the 25th and 75th and the 5th and 95th percentiles of those means over the worlds that still have a value there (a world that died has none after its death).\n\n**To make it again:** `python3 book_figures.py extremes`."
  },
  "stars": {
   "title": "Worlds held together by one agent",
   "caption": "Left: after every game, the connections of the best-connected agent divided by the agents alive, in the worlds whose best-connected agent held, on average over iterations 500\u20131,499, a tenth of the world or more (one line each), and in the other worlds (the line is the median of the worlds at each iteration, the darker band holds the middle half of them (from the 25th to the 75th percentile) and the paler band nine in ten (5th to 95th)). Right: one dot per world, its mean over the settled life of that share and of the share of agents in the core ([Core, trees and leaves](../notes/core-trees-leaves.md)), for the worlds of 100,000 tokens (blue) and of 10,000 (yellow, over iterations 500\u20132,999).",
